# Story page: chaos
# {name} becomes the snake's name. Paragraphs are separated by a blank line.
title = The Orchard Storm
---
The sky split open and apples fell like rain, if rain were delicious and struck you on the head at considerable speed.

{name} ate, and ate, and ate, and for one glorious moment was the fastest and fullest snake in recorded history. I did not record it. I was hiding under a bench.

In the eye of the storm a thousand lights blinked at once and whispered {name}'s name. They pronounced it wrong. When the universe calls your name, it rarely gets it right.
